Z||000010||84Bill||05-09-2001||03:59 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fleabitdog:<BR><B>84Bill<P>I don't have a cell phone, Can you just get on and wait along the pike? We will look for you. Dave</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I can hang out at the first rest stop on the NE extension if no one has a phone.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||84Bill||05-09-2001||05:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric_PA:<BR><B>It also needs a 4 wheel alignment since I redid all the suspension. Don't want to ruin the new tires. I guess I could take my 84, but it is in poor condition.<P>Eric</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Backyard alignment will work ok. <BR>Run a fishin line from the front tire to the back tire so it just touches the side wall of both. then adjust the front (steering wheel straight) wheel until the string just touches the front and rear side walls of the front then do the rear and then adjust a wee bit more on the front. do both sides and you will be surprised how close to the proper settings you will be. It's not perfect but it beats looking out the passanger window while going down the road and you won't burn your tires up real bad.||||reg||1
